Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 54 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FIBROMATOSIS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The margins of the specimen appear free of fibromatosis  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF FIBROMATOSIS  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   UNREMARKABLE LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 06 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen  with a long suture and a short suture at right angle  with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm skin and nipple with a diameter of 1 2cm  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a central REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm mass with a tan homogenous surface  Sections are submitted from margin adjacent to long suture in cassette A and B  B representing regions immediately adjacent to skin  Section code  C  tissue across from long suture involving margins D  tissue immediately adjacent to short suture E  tissue across from short suture F  section through deep margin where tumor is closest to surgical margin  approximately 1 0cm G  additional section through lesion H  section through nipple  Received fresh in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior margin skin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm of oriented tan skin with underlying subcutaneous tissue  Oriented with the long and short suture  The deep aspect of the specimen is inked in black  The region distal to short sutures inked in green  The specimen is submitted serially  starting from the long suture in cassettes I through K  with the short suture sliced in cassette K  Received fresh in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  enlarged  axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan  firm  lymph node  bisected and submitted entirely in cassette L  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  James Warren May Jr   M D  Lawrence T Geoghegan  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  SKIN  RI