00 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty tissue fragment inked and sectioned to reveal a white  firm  ill defined stellate nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  extending grossly to an inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  Representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes A through D  with two representative sections of uninvolved parenchyma in cassettes E and F  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA PRESENT AT MARGIN  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION   report_end  , No.
