is red yellow and fatty and without gross lesions  A stitch marks the 12 00 position  The anterior surface is inked blue  and the posterior black  Upon sectioning the specimen there is a cavity consistent with biopsy cavity inferior to the nipple  which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  The 1 0cm surrounding the tissue is firm and is white tan and somewhat distinct from the surrounding yellow fatty breast parenchyma  The fibrous tissue and biopsy cavity is remote from the superior  inferior  medial  lateral  and posterior  deep  margin  The tissue and biopsy cavity are 0 5cm from the anterior margin  At the point that is closest to the anterior margin  there is overlying skin  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple and underlying biopsy cavity and fibrous region adjacent to biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin and underlying closest relationship to biopsy cavity from lateral portion of biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of region parallel to biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin and underlying closest relationship to medial portion of biopsy cavity and fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of medial deep portion of biopsy cavity and surrounding fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Involved tissue from margin deep to biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative tissue from medial portion of specimen that is somewhat fibrous   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section from lateral portion of specimen that is somewhat fibrous  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left sentinel node  are two tan red soft tissue fragments  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The smaller tissue is inked black  and both fragments are frozen as FX 1  now resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left mastectomy flap  are three skin ellipses measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The tissue is unoriented  The tissue consists of white skin and underlying red pink fatty soft tissue  The underlying deep surface of each skin ellipse is inked black  The deep surface of the small ellipse fragment is over inked yellow  Two representative sections of the largest skin fragment are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two representative sections of each of the smallest two fragments are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION 1  LEFT SENTINEL NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Gross Dictation by Alton Brad Farris III M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Alton Brad Farris III M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by James R Stone M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Less than 10  of in situ tumor cells stain faintly for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   FLAP 