Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Breast  partial mastectomy  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  MEHRA GOLSHAN M D   CASE  BS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Resident  Christopher P  Elco  M D   Ph D   Marianna B Ruzinova  M D   Ph D   Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST  SIMPLE PROPHYLACTIC MASTECTOMY   Benign nipple and breast tissue with calcifications  Fibroadenoma  RIGHT BREAST  MASTECTOMY  AND AXILLARY LYMPH NODE DISSECTION  LEVELS ONE AND  TWO  TWO SPECIMENS    DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  clinging type  high nuclear grade  without  necrosis or calcifications  is present in the tumor bed in the upper outer  quadrant  in the lower outer quadrant  and involves the lactiferous sinuses  of the nipple  8 of 18 blocks   see note    No lymphovascular invasion is identified  The nipple and skin are free of carcinoma   The deep margin is free of carcinoma   Eighteen axillary lymph nodes are free of carcinoma  There is no  evidence of prior tumor involvement  see note    NOTE  The patient presented with two palpable irregular masses located  approximately 3 0cm apart and measuring 1 7cm and 2 0cm  Core needle  biopsies of both masses revealed poorly differentiated invasive ductal  carcinoma  morphologically similar in both locations   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The  carcinoma was negative for ER and PR and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu positive  Core needle  biopsy of the second mass also revealed high grade comedo and cribriform DCIS  associated with necrosis   MRI revealed a large irregular area of highly suspicious rapid  enhancement involving most of the upper breast  predominantly present  in the upper outer quadrant  but extending into the upper inner breast   The overall area of involvement was estimated to be at least 7 x REMOVED_DATE x  4 5cm  A round suspicious appearing lymph node was present caudal to  the tumor in the lower slightly outer breast posteriorly  Suspicious  retropectoral lymph nodes were seen and several right axillary lymph  nodes appeared enlarged  There was no enhancement of the underlying  pectoralis muscle  or evidence of involvement of the skin  A fine  needle aspiration of a right axillary node was positive for metastatic  carcinoma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     The patient was treated with neoadjuvant chemotherapy using Taxotere   carboplatin and Herceptin  She had a complete clinical and  radiological response   Grossly  no area in the mastectomy specimen was suspicious for invasive  carcinoma  Two clips marking the prior core needle biopsy sites were  identified  The tissue around the clips shows stromal fibrosis and DCIS  consistent with the tumor bed  No residual invasive carcinoma is  seen   The residual DCIS is similar in nuclear grade to the pretreatment DCIS   However  the cells are present as a single layer and do not fill the  ducts   The lymph nodes are free of carcinoma  No fibrous scarring is present   The patient has had a pathologic complete response to treatment and  would be classified as Miller Payne response score of 5 and Residual  Cancer Burden  RCB  class 0   This carcinoma would be classified as AJCC  6th edition  y Tis  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    CLINICAL DATA   History  49 year old female with locally advanced right breast cancer  s p  neoadjuvant chemotherapy  Complete clinical and imaging response   Operation  Left breast simple mastectomy and right breast modified radical  mastectomy   Operative Findings  Not provided   Clinical Diagnosis  Left breast   high risk of cancer and right breast cancer   s p neoadjuvant therapy   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Left breast simple mastectomy  short suture superior  long  suture superior   B 2  Right breast simple mastectomy  short suture superior  long  suture lateral   C 3  Right axillary contents  Levels I and II   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh  in three parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATI