Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Amend Addenda  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Breast  mastectomy with regional lymph nodes  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  ESTHER RHEI M D   CASE  BS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME              Addended Report              Resident  Marianna B Ruzinova  M D   Ph D   Jane E Brock  M B   B S   Ph D   Pathologist  Deborah A Dillon  M D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST  MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY LYMPH NODE DISSECTION S P NEOADJUVANT  CHEMOTHERAPY   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  moderately to poorly differentiated  modified  Bloom Richardson grade II III III  see NOTE    Extensive lymphovascular invasion is present  multiple foci  multiple blocks    No definite dermal lymphatic invasion is seen  see note    DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  solid and cribriform types  intermediate to high  nuclear grade   with focal calcifications  is present as a minor component  EIC  negative    Deep margin in negative for carcinoma  Skeletal muscle is present and shows no  involvement by carcinoma   METASTATIC CARCINOMA is present in eight of ten axillary lymph nodes  The  largest metastatic deposit measures 2 7cm  Extranodal extension is present   Seven of the eight positive lymph nodes show at least focal fibrosis compatible  with treatment effect   Note  The patient presented with an area of diffuse enhancement measuring 10cm  on MRI with masses in the axillary tail measuring 4cm and 3cm  Following  neoadjuvant chemotherapy  the area of diffuse enhancement measured 5cm on MRI   Gross examination revealed a 9 0cm ill defined area of nodular fibrosis as  well as two masses in the axilla measuring 2 7cm and 1 4cm  Microscopically   foci of residual invasive carcinoma are seen throughout all sections sampled  from the 9cm fibrous area and the two axillary masses are seen to represent  lymph node metastases  Histologic findings are compatible with a grade 3  response in the Miller Payne system  