Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 41 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENSIVE  MULTIPLE MICROSCOPIC FOCI  GRADE 3  FOCALLY PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP AND ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGINS AND WITH EXTENSIVE BLOOD AND LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The invasive tumor is extensive  in a multifocal pattern  Thus  the exact overall size is difficult to determine with great accuracy  the invasive tumor is probably greater than 3 5cm in overall dimension  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 25     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 07 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 15 x 11 x 3cm unoriented mastectomy specimen with an overlying eccentric REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm unremarkable white skin ellipse with a central  grossly unremarkable nipple areola complex  There is an eccentric 1 5cm linear puckering which is consistent with a healed scar  Sectioning beneath this region reveals firm  focally gritty parenchyma which is mildly hemorrhagic and ill defined measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  This ill defined area is composed predominantly of dense  white fibrous tissue intermixed with the aforementioned abnormalities  The gritty and nodular foci come within between 0 1cm and 0 5cm from the closest margin  deep resection margin   The adjacent parenchyma  mid portion of the specimen  has focal nodularity measuring up to 0 5cm in greatest dimension which come within 0 3cm of the closest margin  anterior   At the opposite end of the specimen  the end without the overlying skin ellipse   the margin appears grossly unremarkable  Within 1 5cm of that side margin  there are dense  white  nodular foci measuring up to 0 7cm in greatest dimension which come within 0 4cm of the closest margin  anterior   The remaining parenchyma is predominantly unremarkable adipose tissue interspersed with moderate  dense  white fibrous tissue  SECTION CODE A  En face section of margin closest to scar  B  Gritty area of biopsy site in relation to deep margin  C  Hemorrhagic area of biopsy site in relation to deep margin  D E  Nodular areas of biopsy site in relation to deep margin  F H  Central nodularity in relation to closest anterior margin  I J  Nodularity of parenchyma from opposite end of specimen  K  En face margin of end opposite the scar  NOTE  The superior and inferior margins are grossly uninvolved by the previously described lesions by a distance of at least 1 0cm  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  W P Andrew Lee  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , No.
