sis   Micro REMOVED_DATE  black inked margin closest to biopsy site  2 frags  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  red inked margin closest to biopsy site  2 frags  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  blue inked margin with skin closest to biopsy site  2  frags  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  orange inked margin closest to biopsy site  2 frags  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  yellow inked margin closest to biopsy site  2 frags  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  green inked margin closest to biopsy site  2 frags  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen  mult frags  ESS   jhl  Reports to  CARTER  KATHARINE M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  04 AUG 97 at 08 40 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO SEVERAL INKED SURFACES AND WITH FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  Carcinoma in situ is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  06 AUG 97 at 17 45                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 97 at 14 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number and  Left Breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a hard  well defined  tan red REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nodule that abuts the margin of excision  Representative sections of discrete nodule frozen as FX 1  now in A  remainder of nodule frozen in B E  The remainder of parenchyma is white and nodular and submitted entirely in F H  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA O R  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , No.
