ing 11 grams and measuring 4cm from medial to lateral  3  cm from inferior to superior  1 5cm from posterior to anterior  The specimen  is received oriented with two stitches as per surgeon   long stitch is lateral  and short stitch is superior  The specimen is also inked by the surgeon per  pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior   black  anterior    blue  superior   red  inferior   green  lateral   yellow  medial   orange   After sectioning  three areas of firmness are identified  the largest of which  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  This is also the most medial area of firmness   It lies 0 1cm from the anterior margin  0 5cm from the posterior margin and  0 3cm from the inferior margin  The second area is 0 5cm lateral to the  first one and is located 0 5cm from the anterior margin  0 2cm from the  posterior margin and 0 1cm from the inferior margin  The third area is 0 3cm  away from the second one and is 0 2cm from the posterior margin  0 4cm from  the anterior margin and 0 1cm from the inferior margin  The entire specimen  is submitted for histologic evaluation   Micro REMOVED_DATE  right breast biopsy specimen submitted from medial to lateral  the  areas described are present in cassettes 3  5   7   Reports to  RHEI  ESTHER M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS   report_end  , No.
